            <ArticleTitle>Novel technique for diagnosis and management of Fraley's syndrome: helical CT with three-dimensional volume rendering.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>755-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the diagnosis and minimally invasive management of Fraley's syndrome using helical CT with volume-rendering techniques in an 18-year-old patient. Three-dimensional images were generated rapidly and allowed safe planning and execution of a laser infundibulotomy of the upper-pole calix. After 24 months of follow-up, the patient remains pain free.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
